---
title: Create Product Workflow — Sequence Diagram
---
sequenceDiagram
    actor Merchant
    participant AdminAPI as Admin API Route<br/>/admin/products
    participant WF as createProductWorkflow
    participant ValStep as validateProductStep
    participant ProdStep as createProductsStep
    participant PricingStep as createPricingStep
    participant InvStep as attachInventoryItemsStep
    participant ProductSvc as ProductModuleService
    participant EventBus as Event Bus
    participant DB as PostgreSQL

    Merchant->>AdminAPI: POST /admin/products {title, variants, options, prices}
    AdminAPI->>WF: workflow.run(input)

    WF->>ValStep: validate(input)
    ValStep-->>WF: validated input

    WF->>ProdStep: createProducts(validated)
    ProdStep->>ProductSvc: createProducts([data])
    ProductSvc->>DB: BEGIN transaction
    ProductSvc->>DB: INSERT Product (generate handle)
    ProductSvc->>DB: UPSERT ProductType / ProductTags
    ProductSvc->>DB: INSERT ProductOptions
    ProductSvc->>DB: INSERT ProductOptionValues
    ProductSvc->>DB: INSERT ProductVariants
    ProductSvc->>DB: INSERT ProductImages
    ProductSvc->>DB: COMMIT
    ProductSvc->>EventBus: emit product.created (after commit)
    ProdStep-->>WF: ProductDTO[]

    WF->>PricingStep: createPrices(variants, prices)
    PricingStep-->>WF: PriceSetDTO[]

    WF->>InvStep: createInventoryItems(variants)
    InvStep-->>WF: InventoryItemDTO[]

    WF-->>AdminAPI: { product: ProductDTO }
    AdminAPI-->>Merchant: 201 Created

    Note over WF,DB: If any step fails, compensation<br/>runs in reverse: deleteInventoryItems →<br/>deletePrices → deleteProducts
